WEBVTT

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>We don't have enough.</i>

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>Not enough time, not enough strength.</i>

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.330
<i>Hakone Academy High School is strong.</i>

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.320
<i>Izumida, Ashikiba, Kuroda, Manami...</i>

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.490
<i>Just the four of them would be strong 
enough to win a national race.</i>

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.500
<i>Two more will be joining them.</i>

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.900
<i>All six members of Hakone Academy 
High School are aces.</i>

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.750
<i>Kyoto Fushimi High School and Hiroshima 
will be looking for revenge, too.</i>

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.530
<i>Road races aren't so easy that 
just because we won last year,</i>

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.340
<i>we'll win again this year.</i>

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.260
<i>Carrying on and entrusting...</i>

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.650
<i>Our methods stress entrusting 
and being entrusted.</i>

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.060
<i>That goes for six of us.</i>

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.370
<i>We need to be—</i>

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.450
Onoda-san is carsick!

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.700
<b><i>Cycling Sports Center</i></b>

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.610
<i>We'll become stronger...</i>

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.410
<i>At this training camp.</i>

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.350
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.340
<i>RIDE.13  1000km Again</i>

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.210
What?

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.950
You heard me.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.990
You're going to ride a thousand 
kilometers in four days

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.830
on the cycling sports center's circuit course.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:42.930
One thousand?

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.670
We're not going to do two-minute 
sprints or heartbeat training?

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.220
Seriously? Two hundred and fifty
kilometers a day?

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.860
That's insane!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.120
<i>Nice reaction.</i>

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.320
<i>He's easy to read.</i>

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.950
Oh, I know. You're joking, aren't you?

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.690
We're serious.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:02.900
It's for real.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.890
You'll lose consciousness before you finish.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.040
You'll master the ability to 
remain focused while riding.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.280
What?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.630
You're all responsible for managing 
your own physical condition.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.470
If you're tired, rest. I won't 
blame you for dropping out, either.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.640
Ride with a light at night.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.480
We're going to be riding at night?

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.680
Just riding during the day won't be enough.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.640
What should we do, Danchiku?

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.660
Don't worry, Issa. I'm with you.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.150
I appreciate it.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.900
You'll attach a sensor to your bike.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.650
Your rank will be displayed 
on this digital scoreboard.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.510
If you're an Inter-High regular, 
not only do I expect you to finish,

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:45.490
<b>Teshima</b>

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:45.990
<b>Teshima
Aoyagi</b>

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:46.490
<b>Teshima
Aoyagi
Imaizumi</b>

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:46.990
<b>Teshima
Aoyagi
Imaizumi
Naruko</b>

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.200
but at the end of the fourth day...

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:47.490
<b>Teshima
Aoyagi
Imaizumi
Naruko
Onoda</b>

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.200
<b>Teshima
Aoyagi
Imaizumi
Naruko
Onoda
Kaburagi</b>

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.210
I expect you to place in the top six.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.920
We're going so fast.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:58.200
<i>Damn. I knew this wouldn't be an easy 
cycling trip, but this is really hard.</i>

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.920
<i>What is Teshima-san thinking?</i>

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.720
Last year Imaizumi, Naruko, and Onoda

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.150
completed one thousand kilometers 
after modifying their bikes.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.760
Modifying?

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.640
They switched out their shifters, 
handlebars, and wheels.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.020
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.340
I'll be modifying your bike, too.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.020
Yes, sir.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.990
<i>Is it my wheels or gears?</i>

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.400
I haven't done anything to those.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.030
It's you.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.150
What?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.850
Obey the following rule.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:29.490
While riding on the course,
don't get within ten meters of Danchiku.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.980
You're the only one who will 
be riding in the Inter-High.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.370
Danchiku won't be on the Inter-High course.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.740
Both of you ride while wearing these meters.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.590
I've set their sensors to ten meters.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.240
If you approach each other, 
an alarm will sound.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:02.530
Teshima-san...

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.610
What are you going to do 
if we don't finish in the top six?

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.370
You'll be removed from the lineup.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.270
Isn't that a little harsh?

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.910
Showoff seemed depressed.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.430
If he can't make the top six
 under these conditions,

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.790
I'm removing him from the lineup.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.920
Those same conditions apply to us.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.670
<i>Teshima-san and Aoyagi-san 
have the same devices</i>

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:33.640
<i>on their bikes that 
Kaburagi and Danchiku had.</i>

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:39.900
During this training camp, our perfect 
teamwork style, the two-man team...

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:41.520
...will be dissolved.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.780
<i>Dissolved?</i>

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.600
We'll become stronger. We have to.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.530
You know that. We're third-years.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:53.160
But we've still never finished 
a thousand kilometers.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.420
Hey, Onoda.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.470
Kanzaki-san!

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.310
Sorry I'm late. There was traffic.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.880
It's totally fine.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.960
Thank you. I was able to get some rest.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.580
I've got some stuff in the passenger seat.
Ride in the middle.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.760
Okay.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:14.440
Hey.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.430
Koga-senpai...

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.640
I heard you got carsick, too.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.190
Yeah.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.530
<i>My legs feel heavy.</i>

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:26.270
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:31.490
<i>I didn't realize my mental state could 
have such a large effect on my riding.</i>

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.790
<i>It's like they're made of stone.</i>

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.370
I'm asking for your help. During the 
training camp that starts tomorrow...

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.340
Ride with me, Danchiku.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.590
There's something I've come to 
realize during practice lately.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:50.590
Without you, there's no one I can depend 
on when my stomach starts to hurt.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.590
I'm only able to be myself because of you.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.450
<i>This is impossible. A thousand 
kilometers in four days...</i>

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.940
<i>And I have to place in the top six.</i>

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.360
<i>I can't do that on a track 
I have no experience on...</i>

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.870
<i>By myself.</i>

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.030
Danchiku!

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.290
<i>Where's the finish line at the 
end of a thousand kilometers?</i>

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.420
<i>Someone who's never ridden it
 before has no idea.</i>

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.860
<i>I can't imagine the endlessness.</i>

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.420
<i>How many times do I pedal? 
For how many hours?</i>

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:32.300
Ow...

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.560
<i>Ow! My stomach is starting to hurt.</i>

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.800
Answer me, Danchiku.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.240
Save me, Danchiku...

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:43.900
It's now or never! Go, Issa!

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.280
Frolic more, Genius Kaburagi!

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.770
Give me praise. Tell me what to do.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.910
Lift me up, Danchiku!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.860
Oh, right. The training camp.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:11.220
Damn it. The first-year amateurs 
passed me at some point.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.220
That means I'm last!

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.670
D-Damn it. My cleat won't snap in.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:19.350
You're not last.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.850
You're being lapped.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.190
While I was spacing out...

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:29.530
They finished one lap on this 
five-kilometer circuit course!

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.570
Hotshot, you've got some 
pretty lame-looking wheels.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.190
What's wrong? Did you lose your allowance?

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:40.790
Yeah, when I went into town the other day.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.290
Don't worry about it.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:45.450
I feel sorry for you.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.840
But honestly, my wheels look lamer.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.960
Don't worry about me, though.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:52.630
Kaburagi!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:56.670
What's wrong? I thought 
you were going to beat us.

00:08:56.670 --> 00:09:00.500
Pass us! If you place sixth 
at this training camp,

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.470
you won't be any use to us at the Inter-High.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:05.480
It's in!

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.070
Damn, damn...

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:13.070
<i>Catch up! Catch up!</i>

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:21.080
Seriously?

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.080
Issa, are you all right?

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.540
Danchiku.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.550
Danchiku, I don't have confidence.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.720
I'm not confident I can finish 
a thousand kilometers. I...

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:46.890
Danchiku...

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.190
This must be what they call "pressure."

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.910
Now that I'm alone, I finally feel it.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:57.610
The pressure of having to ride
a thousand kilometers...

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.060
You're letting it get to you.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.870
I can't do it.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.700
Frolic, Issa.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.160
I can't.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.040
I have to stop riding.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.920
I see two lights in you.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.710
Two lights I don't have.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:17.810
One is the explosive acceleration that comes 
from your focus before the finish line.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:21.720
The other is your desire to 
beat anyone and everyone.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.720
I'm the oldest of three siblings.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.570
Maybe it's because my younger 
siblings are selfish,

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.730
but I tend to yield at crucial junctures.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.930
As the youngest of four siblings, 
you can do what you want.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:35.720
You've been spoiled.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:39.370
What? Is that really relevant 
right now, Danchiku?

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.160
Until now, you've acquired 
the things you wanted.

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.560
You do whatever it takes to acquire 
the things you really want.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:52.420
Buy it, please! Buy it!

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.420
You never let go until you get what you want.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.250
Is that relevant?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.800
You flip over the shogi board 
when you're about to lose.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.010
You even want to win at rock-paper-scissors.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.200
Wait, Danchiku! What are you talking about?

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:04.790
Are you trying to finish me off 
when I'm already feeling down?

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.640
That mentality, which makes people 
dislike you in everyday life,

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.560
becomes an asset in the competitive world.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.070
When you're pushed to your 
limit and nearly exhausted,

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.400
when your body is screaming,

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.440
your last remaining drop of 
mental strength tries to win.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:23.040
That's talent.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.450
<i>Talent...</i>

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:25.670
That's right.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.200
<i>That's why I dream of you doing great things.</i>

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:32.870
People don't recognize their 
talents for what they are.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.540
To them, it's natural.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.080
Notice it. Work hard.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:44.220
I can't help you, but you 
can do it, Genius Kaburagi.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.870
If you want to win,
you'll find plenty of chances.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:53.600
There's still easily more than 
900 meters left on this course.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.270
<i>Sorry, Danchiku. There was 
something wrong with me.</i>

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.860
<i>I'll do it. I'll show you.</i>

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:01.360
<i>I'll do whatever it takes to 
cross the finish line first!</i>

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:08.010
You recover quickly, too.
That's another one of your talents.

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:12.960
Naruko-kun! Imaizumi-kun!

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.860
Hey, the latecomer's here.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:19.840
Onoda-kun, you're five 
laps behind. Pedal hard.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:22.830
Yeah. I'll have to ride 
more than you guys tonight.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.830
Anyway, that upperclassman's going 
to be riding with us this year.

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.990
He rode here in the van with me.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:29.260
Koga-senpai!

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.660
Koga-senpai?

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:34.520
You mean that third-year with glasses 
who's always messing with machines?

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:39.280
<i>Last year he withdrew from the training 
camp because he said he couldn't keep up.</i>

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.320
It's been two years since 
I've been on this course.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.120
He was really nice in the van.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.200
He was easy to talk to.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.620
<b>Motion Sickness Relief</b>

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.910
Want some? It's for motion sickness.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:52.660
It works.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:57.320
Come to think of it, I heard 
Koga-senpai rode 980 kilometers

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.960
at the training camp they
had when he was a first-year.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.310
<i>Nine hundred...</i>

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:02.550
<i>...and eighty?</i>

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:06.800
<i>He quit riding with just 
twenty kilometers left? Why?</i>

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.460
Imaizumi-kun?

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:12.630
Teshima-san!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.120
Apparently, Koga-senpai is participating.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:17.020
I know.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.900
Why didn't you tell us?

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.360
Were you hoping for a list?

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.830
Don't avoid the question.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:27.720
Koga-senpai didn't skip the 
training camp last year because

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.950
he couldn't keep up, did he?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:32.510
You're right. That wasn't why.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.470
He was injured.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.290
What was that?

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.860
Koga-senpai...

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.050
He created so much wind pressure 
just by riding past us.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.930
This year is my last 
chance at the Inter-High.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.310
I came here because I wanted to participate.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.220
If you're a baby who thinks 
you'll be able to participate

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:04.440
in the Inter-High just by finishing 
this course, step forward.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:08.150
I'll crush you and wear your jersey.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.440
I'll show you the burden of riding 
in the Inter-High... by force.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:18.670
Koga-senpai was in the 
Inter-High two years ago?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:23.080
But wait. Isn't finishing a thousand 
kilometers at this training camp

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.300
one of our team's conditions
for being in the Inter-High?

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.680
That's why Onoda worked himself 
until he was exhausted last year.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:38.230
It was only twenty kilometers, but he 
didn't fulfill the conditions. So why?

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:42.040
To cut to the chase,
there were too many reasons.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.990
Koga shouldn't have ridden in 
the Hiroshima race that year.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.490
It's all in the past now.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.330
There's no point in rehashing it.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:56.410
To me and Aoyagi—no, 
Kinjou-san and the others,

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:59.660
he was a significant member of the team.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:04.120
He was the most promising hope of our year.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.420
Koga-senpai was?

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.130
What's wrong?

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:12.760
Are those jerseys just for show,
Naruko? Kaburagi? Onoda?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.180
<i>Koga-senpai?</i>

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:19.380
Or are you bewildered because the man 
who's always performing maintenance

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:22.570
in the corner of the club room 
is speaking so sharply to you?

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.660
No, not at all.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.230
That's why I wore this.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.990
I didn't think I'd wear it again...

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:34.200
But I'm here with the resolve to wear this.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.450
<i>He's wearing another jersey underneath.</i>

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:39.940
It's the Sohoku High School Inter-High jersey

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:41.580
I wore to the Hiroshima race two years ago.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.790
<i>Seriously? He was in the Inter-High?</i>

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:45.840
<i>Koga-senpai!</i>

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.670
I thought showing you this 
would be the fastest way.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.930
<i>That jersey was in rough shape.</i>

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:57.640
<i>Something must've happened 
at that Inter-High.</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.640
But to be honest, you're no match for me.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.940
What do you mean we're no 
match for you, Koga-senpai?

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:18.230
He's trying to pull ahead!
Let's stick to him, Onoda-kun! Showoff!

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:18.830
Yeah!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:19.330
Yes, sir!

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.320
He's fast.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:31.880
He's pulling like crazy, Naruko-kun.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.640
<i>He's been accelerating like a madman.
 How much faster can he go?</i>

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.730
<i>Just how much strength does he have left?</i>

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:44.350
<i>Come to think of it, 
Kinjou-san said this guy...</i>

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.350
<i>I'm the Stamina Simpleton.</i>

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.230
In middle school?

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:52.360
I never skipped practice and was 
always the last one to quit,

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.690
so I had a weird nickname.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:56.700
They called me the Stamina Simpleton.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:59.620
That's a good nickname.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.750
It's simple and single-minded.

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:06.710
Kinjou-san praised my nickname.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.090
You came, Koga.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>He accelerated so he could catch up.</i>

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:23.020
We need you. That's why I said 
you were no match for me.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:29.230
The man I'm trying to knock out at 
this training camp is you, Teshima.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.900
<i>Teshima-san?</i>

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:40.790
Onoda, you know who's the weakest 
member of the current Inter-High team.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.330
I'm weak.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:49.010
Let's race, Teshima. Switch with me.

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.840
I'll become the new captain.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.090
<i>He's challenging Teshima-san?</i>

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:58.520
He should've told you before 
this training camp started

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:01.100
that he'd cut anyone who 
didn't place in the top six.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:05.220
It's because he knew I was coming.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.190
You'd better be ready for this.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:12.160
Imaizumi, Naruko, Onoda, Kaburagi... Sorry.

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:15.550
I lied when I said I'd chosen the lineup.

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.450
I'm the only one who's not a sure thing.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:22.960
<i>His roar is deafening.</i>

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.040
The old you would've fallen to that!

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.290
Koga!

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:34.050
It's been a while since we 
last raced all out, Junta!

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.920
This is my first time!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.630
I always fell behind when 
we used to ride together!

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:42.050
Are you over your injury?

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:46.890
Yeah. I lost a year and a half because of it.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.790
But I've made a complete recovery.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:52.690
I made sure I did, so I could 
ride in my last Inter-High!

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:56.690
Switch with me, Teshima! I can 
make Sohoku High School stronger!

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.630
A Sohoku of strength!

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:00.610
That's my plan for the team.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.650
I'll make Aoyagi and 
Naruko ride on the flats.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.130
I'll have Kaburagi assist.

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.120
Onoda will take the mountains.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.160
Imaizumi and I will handle the finish line.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.670
We can achieve a consecutive 
championship this way!

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:15.040
Don't worry. It won't take long for me 
to get along with the other members.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.670
I know them well.

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:22.010
I've been watching them from 
the corner of the club room.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:26.620
It must've been hard bringing 
that prickly group together.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:30.310
But it's all right now. Leave the rest to me.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.830
Don't worry about me.
I'm doing this because I want to.

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:36.320
I don't have any intention 
of handing it over to you!

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:39.610
Isn't that why we're racing 
a thousand kilometers, Koga?

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.820
Teshima!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.880
Wait, what?

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:45.410
Is our captain changing?

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.160
But we couldn't have won the 
preliminaries without Teshima-san.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:52.460
After watching him ride, 
Koga-senpai seems honestly—

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:53.570
After them!

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:54.240
Yeah!

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.660
Of course!

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:59.420
<i>Regardless of who wins,
we have to see this through.</i>

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:02.750
<i>"I'm the only one who's not a sure thing"?
What's he showing off for?</i>

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.470
<i>A race? Is he serious?</i>

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.470
<i>The way that glasses guy
rode was something else!</i>

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:09.970
<i>Teshima will lose!</i>

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:11.740
<i>This is Teshima-san we're talking about.</i>

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.670
<i>He must have a plan.</i>

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:15.980
<i>Something surprising. He must.</i>

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.440
<i>So why do I have a bad feeling about this?</i>

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:24.140
Teshima, it's 800 meters 
to the starting line.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:29.200
Show me how much faster your
once-ordinary riding has become.

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:33.340
Don't bother holding back. Let me be clear.

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.960
I won't let you finish a thousand kilometers.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.380
I'll tear it from you.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.590
I'll corner you through brute force.

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:43.470
I'm going to make you drop out.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:44.760
Four hundred meters left!

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.180
They're getting ready to sprint.

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:50.890
Is the distance to the starting 
line their first test of strength?

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:51.680
Teshima-san...

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:56.560
He jumped ahead! He's got it!

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:00.650
<i>You've gotten stronger. 
I hardly recognize you.</i>

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.340
<i>But you're still...</i>

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.150
<i>Ordinary!</i>

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:16.830
That's how strong you are.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:18.750
Feel like giving up yet?

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:25.140
Looks like there won't be any time for 
tea until I finish a thousand kilometers.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.660
You always had to have the last word.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:31.260
I said I'd make you drop out.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.520
I'll push you until you can't talk anymore.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:38.520
I'm the guy known as the Stamina Simpleton.

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:15.160
Kaburagi-kun, Danchiku-kun...

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:19.080
Kanzaki-san gave these to me before we 
left this morning so we could share them.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.310
What? The manager?

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:22.830
They're from a girl?

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:24.560
I don't want any!

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:26.250
Why not? They're good.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:29.110
It'd be a waste, Issa. No one's watching.

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:34.090
I don't want any!

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:36.050
<i>What is he, a kid?</i>

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT RIDE  The Ordinary Man and the Genius</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:51.000
<b><i>The high cadence
 continues!!</i></b>
